{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block main %}
<h1>Quantum Phantoms <span class="live" title="This page is regenerated as the work progresses; states, ratings and numbers change.">(live document)</span></h1>
<p class="live-note">Live document: it tracks the progress of the reverse-engineering work and is rebuilt from the
letter READMEs and <code>status.json</code> as targets move. States, ratings and numbers will change.</p>
<p class="lede"><strong>What we aim to achieve:</strong> synthetic lung tumours inside real 3-D chest CT that are
realistic enough to train cancer-detection AI, controlled enough to test it on exactly the cases it misses, and
traceable enough that a clinician or regulator can trust the result.</p>

<p><strong>Why it matters.</strong> Detection models fail most on the cases real data has least of: tiny,
ground-glass, and wall- or vessel-touching nodules, usually without exact ground truth, follow-up scans or the right
to share them. Synthetic tumours with exact masks, chosen difficulty and a baseline and follow-up scan can fill that
gap without using any patient voxels. They are only trustworthy if every step rests on a published, reproduced method
and every case can be traced back to how it was made. If the pipeline reaches clinical validation, it can bring
better-trained and better-tested lung-cancer detection forward by a few years.
<span class="chip extrapolation">extrapolation</span></p>

<p><strong>Why quantum.</strong> The plan is to build one large quantum circuit that maps how a tumour starts growing:
in D the first cell lineage and tissue patch grow through entangled quantum dynamics on IBM's heavy-hex chip. It runs
at 21 qubits in simulation today; the planned 108-qubit version aims beyond classical simulation (claim level L2,
<a href="{{ root }}site/future.html#planned-l2-in-d-at-108-qubits">plan and conditions</a>).
<span class="chip speculative">speculative</span>
C certifies every tumour draw with a Bell test, and B draws site and tumour type together in one quantum circuit.
<span class="chip evidence">evidence-based</span></p>

<p><strong>Disclaimer.</strong> At today's sizes the quantum stages can still be simulated classically, on laptops or
supercomputers, so this work builds a quantum pipeline that is ready when hardware outgrows them. See the
<a href="{{ root }}site/future.html">Future</a> and its
<a href="{{ root }}site/future.html#disclaimer-what-quantum-is-allowed-to-mean-here">claim ladder</a>.</p>

<h2 id="pipeline">Pipeline readiness</h2>
{% set box = {"C": [20, 20, "certify"], "A": [270, 20, "place"],
              "B": [520, 20, "draw"], "D": [770, 20, "grow_q"],
              "E": [20, 230, "grow_c"], "F": [270, 230, "render"],
              "G": [520, 230, "commit/sign"], "H": [770, 230, "validate"]} %}
{% set edges = [["C>A", "M190,70 L268,70", 196, 62, "seed"], ["A>B", "M440,70 L518,70", 448, 62, "sites"],
                ["B>D", "M690,70 L768,70", 698, 62, "draw"], ["D>E", "M855,120 L855,170 L105,170 L105,228", 560, 164, "seed_shape (+ draw, cert)"],
                ["E>F", "M190,280 L268,280", 194, 272, "trajectory"], ["F>G", "M440,280 L518,280", 450, 272, "hybrid"],
                ["G>H", "M690,280 L768,280", 696, 272, "receipt"], ["A>F", "M355,120 L355,228", 361, 205, "anatomy_masks"],
                ["B>G", "M605,120 L605,228", 611, 205, "job records (B, C, D)"]] %}
<div class="figure">
<svg class="pipe" viewBox="0 0 960 350" role="img" aria-labelledby="pipe-title">
  <title id="pipe-title">Chain order with each letter coloured by pipeline readiness; dashed red edges are the weakest links</title>
  <defs><marker id="head" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z"/></marker>
  <marker id="head-weak" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z"/></marker></defs>
  {% for e in edges %}<path class="arrow{% if e[0] in weak_edges %} edge-weak{% endif %}" d="{{ e[1] }}"/>
  <text class="lbl{% if e[0] in weak_edges %} edge-weak{% endif %}" x="{{ e[2] }}" y="{{ e[3] }}">{{ e[4] }}</text>
  {% endfor %}
  {% for L, b in box.items() %}<a href="{{ root }}site/{{ (letters | selectattr("letter", "equalto", L) | first).folder }}/index.html">
  {% set c = cards | selectattr("letter", "equalto", L) | first %}
  <g class="node ready-{{ ready[L] }}"><title>{{ L }} · {{ c.step }} · {{ c.folder }}/ · {{ c.n }} target{{ "s" if c.n != 1 }} · {{ ready_labels.get(ready[L], "unrated") }}</title><rect x="{{ b[0] }}" y="{{ b[1] }}" width="170" height="100" rx="10"/>
    <text class="letter" x="{{ b[0] + 14 }}" y="{{ b[1] + 32 }}">{{ L }}</text><text class="out" x="{{ b[0] + 42 }}" y="{{ b[1] + 28 }}">stage: {{ b[2] }}</text>
    <text class="name" x="{{ b[0] + 14 }}" y="{{ b[1] + 60 }}">{{ (letters | selectattr("letter", "equalto", L) | first).step }}</text>
    <text class="rating" x="{{ b[0] + 14 }}" y="{{ b[1] + 84 }}">{{ ready_labels.get(ready[L], "unrated") }}</text></g></a>
  {% endfor %}
</svg>
</div>
<ul class="key">
  {% for r in ["not-ready", "prototype", "caveats", "production"] %}<li><span class="swatch ready-{{ r }}-box"></span>{{ ready_labels[r] }}</li>
  {% endfor %}<li><span class="line"></span>contract file passed on</li>
  <li><span class="line weak"></span>weakest link</li>
</ul>


<h2 id="see">See each step</h2>
<p class="legend">Images already produced by each step. <span class="chip kind-ct">real CT</span> shows real LIDC
chest-CT pixels; <span class="chip kind-phantom">phantom</span> is a synthetic or stub volume;
<span class="chip kind-plot">plot</span> is a chart of the measured result. Click an image for full size.</p>
<div class="gallery">
{% for g in gallery %}
  <section class="g-step">
    <h3><span class="g-letter">{{ g.letter }}</span> {{ g.step }} <a class="g-more" href="{{ root }}site/{{ g.folder }}/index.html">details →</a></h3>
    <div class="g-items">
    {% for it in g["items"] %}
      <a class="g-item g-{{ it.kind }}" href="{{ root }}{{ it.href }}"><img src="{{ root }}{{ it.href }}" alt="{{ it.caption }}" loading="lazy">
        <span class="g-cap"><span class="chip kind-{{ it.kind }}">{{ it.kind_label }}</span> {{ it.caption }}</span></a>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
{% endfor %}
</div>

{% include "explainer.html.j2" %}

<h2 id="targets">All targets</h2>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table class="targets">
  <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Letter</th><th>Target</th><th>Priority</th><th>Kind</th><th>State</th><th>Claim</th><th>Sim</th><th>Reproduced</th><th>Papers</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for r in rows %}
    <tr>
      <td class="num">{{ r.number }}</td>
      <td><a href="{{ root }}site/{{ r.folder }}/index.html">{{ r.letter }}</a></td>
      <td><a href="{{ root }}{{ r.href }}">{{ r.name }}</a></td>
      <td class="stars">{{ r.priority | stars }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.kind }}</td>
      <td><span class="badge state-{{ r.state }}" {% if r.rejection_reason %}title="{{ r.rejection_reason }}"{% endif %}>{{ r.state }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ r.claim_level or "—" }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.sim_mode or "—" }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.reproduced_text }}</td>
      <td class="papers">{{ r.papers | join(", ") or "—" }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="legend">States: listed → dissected → reproduced (published number matched) → adapted → integrated | rejected (reason recorded).
Claim levels: L0 provenance · L1 entangled generative state · L1′ quantum memory advantage. Every quantum number is simulated.</p>

